From 28b5e68272b8043cb052d391bd6a7d7fbb52570d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:44:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] refactor(sim): the field column read from below -
 march_up, the mirrored sliver law, the shell-crossing read (#637 E2b)

`SdfField::column_span` reads a column from both sides. The top stays
`march`'s descent; the floor is `march_up`'s ascent (new `march_up.rs`,
the mirror of `march`/`refine`: same keyed probe and budgets, descending
to the LOWEST material centre and reading the floor from `cut_downs` -
a flipped bake's `cut_ups` records moved whole - or the shell's lowest
crossing in the bracket, the higher binding). A field with no
`cut_downs` keeps E1's monotone law with no ascent, so the upright path
is byte-identical in value and cost.

Both marches now read an uncut surface from the cached parity column's
crossing inside the bracket (`march::shell_in`, `march::face`) instead
of the cell boundary, exact to rounding for any plane - a flipped stock
bottom is not lattice-aligned in general. A sign flip with neither a
crossing nor a record (a flipped bounded tool's bottom face) is
`Unreadable`, never the boundary as a guess; on an upright field it
cannot occur (every proven-inside cell records entry 0, and the cell
under it a finite entry).

The sliver law (no material centre) is one scan over adjacent air-centre
pairs from the cell under the shell floor to the one over its ceiling:
the lower centre's `cut_ups` entry is the upper cut's bottom, the upper
centre's `cut_downs` entry is the lower cut's top, the shell binds where
no record does, and a centre proven inside a cut is that cut's whole
half-line. It reads E1's floor sliver, its mirror under a flipped cut,
and a sliver floating between a cut from below and one from above.

E2a's interim refusal (`bounded_cuts` on a flipped bake) is lifted; the
flag follows the tool alone. `floor_at` keeps its API. Column-engine
verdicts, goldens and snapshots are unchanged.

Pinned by field_floor (the exact read where the interim refusal was
pinned, the flipped through-slot, the mirrored sliver, the flipped
bounded tool's refusal, an unaligned plane read on both sides) and
carry_engine_agreement (the baked read-back bit-for-bit with the view
through all 8 turns, flips included; an unaligned block top; the slots
cut before and after a flip - two-sided columns, a sliver between the
two cuts, a cut through the first - agreeing with the column engine per
column to 1e-6).

Fixes #780

