From 03437938a1e013ec19a82ab515523ab0fca7a5d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:18:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(sim): a centre-less floor skin is a verdict on every
 march path, never NaN

The second review of #817 found that `march::walk` answered `NoMaterial`
for a column whose remaining skin held no cell centre (a plate -6.05..0
at cell 0.5 with a slot at -5.8 leaves [-6.05, -5.8] between the air
centre at -6.25 and the claimed centre at -5.75). Every verdict reader
that marches alone - `Stock::top`, `deviate`, `measure`, the sheet and
the column masks - read that as NaN: the rest under the slot vanished
from the report and the rest mask would have treated the steel as air.
Only `column_span` read such skins, through `field_floor`'s sliver law.

The walk now reads a centre-less column itself before it ever answers
"no material", through the one sliver law (`field_floor::sliver`, shared,
with the shell's extent from the new `shell_extent`): a column the shell
never crosses is air, a sliver the records place answers its top (a
descent) or floor (an ascent), one the records prove cut through is
`NoMaterial`, and one that cannot be placed is `Unreadable` - never
`NoMaterial` where the shell says material stands. The mesh-only walk
answers the shell's highest or lowest crossing. `column_span`'s own
`NoMaterial => sliver` arm becomes `Empty`.

Pinned by the new `field_skin` suite: the reviewer's scenario through
`Stock::top`, `deviate` (192 of 192 columns rest, 0 NaN), `Columns` and
the flipped stock; and a sweep of 6 floors x 3 tops x 12 slot depths
(skins 0.01-0.3), upright and flipped, through `Stock::top`, the flipped
`column_span` and `deviate` - 1296 reads, 1296 exact, no NaN, no refusal
(186 NaN reads and 81 NaN deviate runs on the previous head). Both pins
fail on the unfixed source; the round-1 pins stay green.

