From 8ed831b7a8b14d99d42e05fb05338013c420e20b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:57:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(sim): cuts through a carried field in the new frame
 (#637 E2c)

CarriedField::simulate bakes the view's signed permutation into the
bricks (SdfField::turned) on the first cut after a turn, shifts every
move by the residual translation (from, to, and the arc centre in its
plane's word order) and cuts through simulate_field - the field arm of
Stock::simulate moved into one function, so later cuts ride the shipped
+Z tool construction (spanning_flank, batched per brick): true XY arcs,
the closed-form flat floor. The clip stays at read-back; column_body
reads through column_span.

CarriedField keeps a sticky `flipped` flag (new, then): a baked flip
leaves only a translation as the view, and two composed flips an upright
one, yet the floor has faced the spindle - Body::carry's own law.

carry_engine_agreement runs #780's by-hand cut-after-flip pins through
the real simulate and grows an XY arc after the flip and a second carry
(quarter turn; flip back) after a cut; both engines agree per column on
empty_at, top and floor to 1e-6 and on floor_judged. field_carry pins
simulate bit for bit against the by-hand bake and shift through all 8
turns (XY and XZ arcs), the refusal-before-bake order, and the flag.

Fixes #781

